invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont.c
catches: rsa_ifma_model_test
reason: rsa_mont.c's use_ifma answers 0 whatever the session's ch_cfg.cpu
  says, so no session runs the AVX-512 IFMA kernel and CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA
  picks nothing. Every byte stays right, because rsa_mont64.c computes
  the same bytes; only the time is wrong. bin/rsa_ifma_model_test counts
  the calls rsa_vp1_cpu makes into rsa_ifma_public over the lane model
  and requires one under the bit for every modulus the kernel takes.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA) != 0;
--- new
    (void)cpu;
    return 0;
